LMAIN.C/nextarg()
	until C86 is ansi, an argument file on 8086 must be read with agetc()
	created a macro GETC for this
7/8/91
	merged in mac changes

7/20/91
	linker didn't report an error when an overlay's initialized data 
	contained a pointer to an overlay function. For example, the linker
	should report an error if the following code is in an overlay:
	  void ov(void){}
	  void (*fp)(void)=ov;

8/16/91
	findsym() was assuming a string list entry was a symbol, and indirecting
	off its sg_sym pointer. This caused enforcer hits on the amiga when program
	was linked with debugging info turned on.
	Added check to make sure it is a symbol.

8/21/91
	when linking in amiga object modules, linker was generating 
	incorrect 32-bit code-to-data relocation records 
